				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tirantal" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1222738); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1222738&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349718" alt="Tirantal" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1222738)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tirantal" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1222738); return false;" >Tirantal</a></span> <span class="odate time_1324492832 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Dec 2011 18:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1332818">
									

<p>Like I said, it's a very minor thing, but I think it would help in immersion. What it comes down to is do you want your readers to smile at that moment? Since the Queen hasn't had character development yet, anything that we hear from her is going to influence the perception we make. I would expect Vector (just as a random example) to be spouting lines from cool movies, so it wouldn't break immersion for her. If that is also what you want to develop as the Queen's schtick, then it should be kept in and maybe enhanced in the further stories.</p>

							</div>

								
					
