			<div class="content" id="post-content-1332829">
									

<p>I was just rereading, and came across one other bit. &quot;There's no audio in this version&#8230;&quot; but then the presenter talked about what questions were being asked of Penbry. After thinking about it for a bit, I realized that this version meant the copy that was being shown, but the need to think it over may be a weakness. Perhaps have the presenter say something like &quot;I've turned down the audio, if you don't mind sir. I don't think hearing Penbry scream is that useful to the brief&quot;. It would also play up the unsettling nature of the tape, if a Foundation agent is disturbed enough to need it off.</p>

