					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(172464); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=172464&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349718" alt="Dr Gears" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=172464)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-gears" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(172464); return false;" >Dr Gears</a></span> <span class="odate time_1324556595 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Dec 2011 12:23</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1333283">
									

<p>Unfortunately, I don't have a lot of ways to avoid tropes, really. Almost every concept under the sun has been done, somehow, so it's just the nature of the beast, at this point. I may head up another angle&#8230;one where she never becomes the Black Queen&#8230;and stumbles in to the same event that cracked Gears all those years ago. More of a Lovecraft-y bend to that one, I think, and i love exploring alternate universes anyway.</p>
<p>I plan on giving her some more challenging bits&#8230;this initial bit is really just a first move. She didn't even know the name of The Foundation before she got hold of Penbry, and stumbled in to MC&amp;D almost by accident&#8230;now that she has more information, she's going to do things a little more forcefully.</p>
<p>Sorry it doesn't quite mesh with you, but i hope it's at least neat in concept.</p>

							</div>

								
					
